  "frap": {
    "status": "implemented",
    "tier": "T1",
    "support": "partial",
    "support_note": "Object Mode and mesh Edit Mode; mirror (mesh symmetry) and snapping options change nothing; the Affect Only Origins/Parents tool settings are not implemented",
    "headless": "native",
    "planned": "M8",
    "extension": false,
    "notes": [
      "In Object Mode only locations change: Blender shears each object's location channel about the world-space pivot.",
      "orient_axis_ortho is the direction that moves, by tan(angle) times the coordinate along orient_axis_ortho × orient_axis; passing both axes equal is degenerate and moves everything onto the pivot, as in Blender."
    ]
  }
